and suppresses singular verb forms. Irregular plurals, plural pronouns and
ambiguous endings provide weaker evidence. Small additional responses cover
punctuation, identifier boundaries and productive s-initial noun suffixes.
Only a trailing word fragment is remembered; documents and line breaks reset
its influence. At the first token, plural-looking words are mildly negative.
