Space chunks around 11-19 characters receive large negative values; chunks
around 28-40 receive positive values. Tabs have their own count profile.
A preceding newline usually lowers the prediction, without crossing documents.
Line endings, nonbreaking spaces and repeated punctuation bars use coarser
curves. All other tokens get exactly zero; weak lexical effects are omitted.
