The negative side recognizes 'als', compact ls/rs/js spellings, and er/ru
syllables in Chinese and Japanese. The positive side recognizes requirements,
dependencies, expectations, opportunities, and README. These are token-piece
rules, not a topic classifier: spelling, case, and leading spaces matter.
Unrecognized tokens receive zero; no preceding context is used.
